From 288a975a1899350c25de9e9c9e89e80599af40c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DUONG TIEN HIEU <tienhieuD@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:23:32 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(xlsx): render xdr:cxnSp connectors with line ends

Root cause: the XLSX drawing parser only acquired `xdr:sp`, `xdr:pic` and
`xdr:grpSp`, so every `xdr:cxnSp` (straight, bent and curved connectors) was
dropped both stand-alone and inside groups, and a straight horizontal or
vertical connector (zero `a:ext` on one axis) was rejected as area-less. The
renderer also never painted `a:headEnd` / `a:tailEnd` decorations, which PPTX
draws through the shared core arrow helpers.

Fix: the parser now treats `cxnSp` like `sp` (ECMA-376 section 20.5.2; the
child spPr/style structure is the same) and lets a connector keep a zero
extent on one axis, filling its anchor along that axis. The XLSX renderer
re-strokes line and bent connectors shortened at decorated ends and draws the
arrow heads with the core helpers used by PPTX (getConnectorAnchors,
traceTrimmedPath, tracePresetLeader, drawArrowHead).

Verification: new Rust unit tests (stand-alone, zero-extent, hidden and
grouped connectors) and vitest renderer tests for arrow decorations; the
parser tests and the arrow test fail without the change. cargo test, cargo
fmt, clippy, tsc, ast-grep lint and the xlsx/core vitest suites pass. Checked
visually with hand-built connector workbooks (straight, bent, curved, flips,
dashes, all end types, oneCellAnchor and grouped).

Not covered: xdr:absoluteAnchor shapes, rotated connectors in stand-alone
anchors, and connectors with compound lines.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Mswwk1DTS2ff66F43iipyG
